#* {{RQ:Fielding Tom Jones|volume=II|book=IV|chapter=The Arrival of a Surgeon. His Operations, and a Long Dialogue between Sophia and Her Maid.|page=103|passage=I aſſure you, my dirty '''Couſin'''! thof his Skin be ſo vvhite, and to be ſure, it is the moſt vvhiteſt that ever vvas ſeen, I am a Chriſtian as vvell as he, and no-body can ſay that I am baſe born, {{...}}|footer=Used disparagingly.}}
#* {{RQ:Scott Tales of the Crusaders|volume=I|chapter=IX|page=174|passage=Marry quep, my '''cousin''' the weaver! And why the cucking-stool, I pray?—because my young lady is comely, and the young squire is a man of mettle, reverence to his beard that is yet to come?|footer=Used disparagingly.}}
